# Outreach drafts pair owner names with phone numbers. Personal data, never
# committed.
#
# The rule lives at the repository root deliberately. It used to live only in
# property-outreach-worker/.gitignore, and `git rm -r` on that folder deleted
# the rule along with it — so the very next `git add -A` staged the previously
# ignored file as a new one and committed it. A root-level rule survives the
# removal of any subfolder.
outreach-drafts/
